   },
   "text": "Passed/agreed to in House: On passage Passed by the Yeas and Nays: 240 - 185 (Roll no. 337).",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36110",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:56:35",
   "recordedVotes": [
    {
     "chamber": "House",
     "congress": 104,
     "date": "1995-05-16T21:56:35Z",
     "rollNumber": 336,
     "sessionNumber": 1,
     "url": "https://clerk.house.gov/evs/1995/roll336.xml"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion to recommit with instructions Failed by the Yeas and Nays: 169 - 256 (Roll no. 336). (consideration: CR H5013)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:27:59",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - The House proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the motion to recommit the bill back to the Committee on Transportation, with instructions.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H36100",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:27:15",
   "committees": [
    {
     "name": "Transportation and Infrastructure Committee",
     "systemCode": "hspw00",
     "url": "https://api.congress.gov/v3/committee/house/hspw00?format=json"
    }
   ],
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Bonior moved to recommit with instructions to Transportation.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H34400",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:26:53",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House adopted the amendment in the nature of a substitute as agreed to by the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H35000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:26:20",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The previous question was ordered pursuant to the rule.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32600",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:25:54",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House rose from the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union to report H.R. 961.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32310",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "17:25:22",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Shuster moved for the Committee of the Whole to rise and report.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "14:14:33",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to an earlier unanimous consent request, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 30 minutes of debate on the Gilchrest amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32050",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "12:35:04",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House resolved into Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union for further consideration.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "12:34:27",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Shuster asked unanimous consent that, during further consideration of the bill in the Committee of the Whole, the time for debate on the pending Boehlert amendment and a proposed Gilchrest amendment, and all amendments thereto be limited to one hour and 30 minutes, respectively. Agreed to without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-16",
   "actionTime": "12:28:14",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4978-5013)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32700",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-15",
   "actionTime": "20:31:41",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union rises leaving H.R. 961 as unfinished business.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-15",
   "actionTime": "20:30:49",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "At the conclusion of debate on the Boehlert amendment the Committee of the Whole rose, leaving unfinished final disposition of the amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32050",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-15",
   "actionTime": "18:03:57",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House resolved into Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union for further consideration.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-15",
   "actionTime": "18:03:47",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4934-4956)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32700",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "12:57:14",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union rises leaving H.R. 961 as unfinished business.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32341",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "12:57:05",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion that the Committee rise Agreed to by voice vote.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32340",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "12:56:46",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Shuster moved that the Committee rise.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "12:32:18",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Boehlert asked unanimous consent to be allowed to reoffer an amendment to Title VI at some point later in the proceedings. Agreed to without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32050",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "10:02:38",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House resolved into Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union for further consideration.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-12",
   "actionTime": "10:02:17",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4875-4900)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32700",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "20:28:09",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union rises leaving H.R. 961 as unfinished business.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32341",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "20:28:00",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "On motion that the committee rise Agreed to by voice vote.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32340",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "20:27:20",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Shuster moved that the committee rise.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "20:22:20",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Chair put the question on the Emerson amendment, as amended, and announced that, by voice vote, the amendment was not agreed to. By unanimous consent, the vote by which the amendment, as amended, was not agreed to was vacated and the Chair again put the question on the Emerson amendment, as amended.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32050",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "10:40:28",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The House resolved into Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union for further consideration.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-11",
   "actionTime": "10:40:16",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered as unfinished business. (consideration: CR H4802-4868)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32700",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "21:52:42",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union rises leaving H.R. 961 as unfinished business.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "18:45:06",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Committee of the Whole proceeded with 45 minutes of debate on the Saxton amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "18:45:05",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Mr. Saxton asked unanimous consent that the time for debate on the Saxton amendment, and all amendments there to, be limited to an additional 45 minutes. Agreed to without objection.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "15:44:57",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 140, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with 10 minutes of debate on the Shuster amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:17:12",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - Pursuant to the provisions of H. Res. 140, the Committee of the Whole proceeded with two hours of general debate.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32400",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:16:37",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable Scott McInnis to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H32020",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:16:36",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 140 and Rule XXIII.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H8D000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:16:26",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 961 with 2 hours of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit. Measure will be read by section. Bill is open to amendments. It shall be in order to consider as an original bill the amendment in the nature of a substitute recommended by the Committee on Transportation now printed in the bill. Amendments previously printed in the Congressional record shall be given priority of consideration. Before consideration of any other amendment it shall be in order to consider the amendment printed in the report accompanying this resolution, debatable for 10 minutes, and not subject to further amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H30000",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:16:21",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 140. (consideration: CR H4690-4788)",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L220",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-10",
   "actionTime": "13:16:18",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rule H. Res. 140 passed House.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
  {
   "actionCode": "H1L210",
   "actionDate": "1995-05-09",
   "actionTime": "15:21:11",
   "sourceSystem": {
    "code": 2,
    "name": "House floor actions"
   },
   "text": "Rules Committee Resolution H. Res. 140 Reported to House. Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 961 with 2 hours of general debate. Previous question shall be considered as ordered without intervening motions except motion to recommit. Measure will be read by section. Bill is open to amendments. It shall be in order to consider as an original bill the amendment in the nature of a substitute recommended by the Committee on Transportation now printed in the bill. Amendments previously printed in the Congressional record shall be given priority of consideration. Before consideration of any other amendment it shall be in order to consider the amendment printed in the report accompanying this resolution, debatable for 10 minutes, and not subject to further amendment.",
   "type": "Floor"
  },
